## 1. Files changed

- `src/new_sort/new_sort.c` — added `-u`/`--unique` support

## 2. Behavior added

`-u`/`--unique` outputs one line from each group of equal sorted lines, retaining the **first input record** from each group. Sorting happens before duplicate removal. The representative selection is independent of sort order (so `-r` reverses group ordering but does not change which representative survives).

## 3. Equality rules

- **Without `-f`**: two lines are unique-equal iff their bytes are identical (same length, `memcmp == 0`).
- **With `-f`**: two lines are unique-equal iff their ASCII case-folded bytes are identical (same length, each byte folded to uppercase and compared). The original-byte secondary comparison used for ordering does **not** participate in uniqueness.

## 4. Option interactions

| Flags | Groups | Representative | Order |
|-------|--------|---------------|-------|
| `-u` | byte-identical | first input record | ascending |
| `-f -u` | case-insensitive | first input record | case-folded ascending |
| `-r -u` | byte-identical | first input record | descending |
| `-r -f -u` | case-insensitive | first input record (same as `-f -u`) | case-folded descending |

